EF AI Workspace (#157): Word and PowerPoint downloads in Aktiv Grotesk, with the logo. Owner decisions 2026-10-23:
embed Aktiv in Word and PowerPoint (a reader without the font gets a read-only file, about 2 MB more per file; Excel
stays Tahoma) and put the logo in the files (the letterhead and date format stay open, #145).

- Brand files (utils/efaiwBrandAssets.ts): Aktiv Regular and Bold, fetched from the platform as they are, and the blue
  and white horizontal logos drawn to PNG from their SVG at print resolution, the viewport sized to the artwork's own
  viewBox. Fetched once per page while a download menu is open; any failure gives the files as before (Tahoma, no logo).
- Word (utils/efaiwDocx.ts): both faces embedded as Word does (obfuscated .odttf, ECMA-376 §17.8.1; font table, the
  embedTrueTypeFonts setting), the styles set in Aktiv, and the blue logo at the top right of the first page, its
  symbol 1.5 cm high with half that as clear space below (guide p9, p13, p17), as in the PDF.
- PowerPoint (utils/efaiwPptx.ts): both faces embedded as Embedded OpenType (.fntdata, the font unchanged after the
  header), the theme and runs in Aktiv, and the white logo at the top right of the title slide.
- The fonts' licence flag (fsType 4, preview and print) is kept: Word and PowerPoint open such a file read-only where
  the font is not installed. LibreOffice ignores embedded fonts that do not allow editing and shows its own.
- The Arabic letter range in efaiwDocx.ts is written with \u escapes (same ranges; eslint no-irregular-whitespace).
- Tests: utils/__tests__/efaiwBrandAssets.test.ts.

